        {
          "id": 2980184650,
          "type": "DiffNote",
          "body": "Hell yeah on Windows, complete with `PCAP_CHAR_ENC_UTF_8`, so that we don't have to worry about non-US-English error messages from Windows being in some random code page (give me CP65001 or give me death).\n\n(And, yes, if you guessed that `pcap_init()` and `PCAP_CHAR_ENC_UTF_8` were put in there at least in part for Wireshark on Windows, you guessed correctly. There's probably code out there written for WinPcap and maybe Npcap that expects current-code-page error messages, so I wanted some way for code that *doesn't* want that not to get that, without breaking programs that really do expect that.)",
