        {
          "id": 3031860113,
          "type": "DiffNote",
          "body": "Thank you for the exhaustive explanation. It sounds as though it's probably not correct to treat Linux differently from all other OSes in dumpcap, but that there's such a mess of different treatments in different OSes that probably the best way to handle it is in libpcap (which has modules for different OSes/drivers/ways of getting packets and thus is closest to understanding it, rather than dumpcap having to understand it), but that involves further thought and work TBD.",
