        {
          "id": 3031875980,
          "type": "DiffNote",
          "body": "In the best of all worlds, for all devices in libpcap\n\n1. non-blocking mode would work;\n2. on non-Windows systems, the device would either provide a selectable file descriptor or a timeout to use in `select()`/`poll()`/etc., and on Windows, it would provide a `HANDLE`;\n3. `pcap_breakloop()` will force a blocking read to wake up.\n\nI'm not sure we live in that world now; it might take some tweaking in OS code to get there.",
